00:39:30,672 --> 00:39:32,848
We just executed
the fucking plan, Joe!

748
00:39:32,848 --> 00:39:33,936
And it worked.

749
00:39:33,936 --> 00:39:34,981
She's back.

750
00:39:34,981 --> 00:39:36,504
And we're a man down.

751
00:39:36,504 --> 00:39:38,506
Man down is the price.

752
00:39:38,506 --> 00:39:40,421
And we all signed up to pay it.

753
00:39:40,421 --> 00:39:41,683
[laughs]

754
00:39:42,771 --> 00:39:44,643
When's the last time
you were in a firefight?

755
00:39:44,643 --> 00:39:47,254
Huh?

756
00:39:47,254 --> 00:39:49,691
And I'm not talking
about some bimbo's bodyguard.

757
00:39:49,691 --> 00:39:52,041
- Fuck you!
- I mean a fucking battle.

758
00:39:53,173 --> 00:39:54,348
It's been a while, hasn't it?

759
00:39:55,305 --> 00:39:56,655
I'll tell you what.

760
00:39:56,655 --> 00:39:58,178
[laughs]

761
00:39:58,178 --> 00:39:59,701
I'll give you another one.

762
00:39:59,701 --> 00:40:00,920
You need an adrenaline dump,

763
00:40:00,920 --> 00:40:03,096
fucking dump it right here.

764
00:40:03,096 --> 00:40:05,533
We're working together now.

765
00:40:05,533 --> 00:40:08,057
You want to do
some fucking cowboy shit,

766
00:40:08,057 --> 00:40:09,929
you do it on your own.

767
00:40:09,929 --> 00:40:12,148
Never fucking do it
with my team.

768
00:40:12,148 --> 00:40:14,455
You know what I would be doing
if I were you?

769
00:40:14,542 --> 00:40:16,718
[laughs] I ca--
I can't wait to hear this.

770
00:40:17,719 --> 00:40:20,635
I'd be calling
that family you got.

771
00:40:24,944 --> 00:40:26,772
You're right.

772
00:40:26,772 --> 00:40:28,643
That's exactly
what I should be doing.

773
00:40:35,824 --> 00:40:37,173
- That should be enough.
- [Kate] It's sticky.

774
00:40:37,173 --> 00:40:39,219
- You just, like, spread it all--
- [phone buzzing]

775
00:40:39,219 --> 00:40:41,656
It's not sticking
to the pan, Dad.

776
00:40:41,656 --> 00:40:42,962
Hey.

777
00:40:43,049 --> 00:40:44,833
[Joe]
<i>Hey.</i>

778
00:40:44,920 --> 00:40:46,182
You okay?

779
00:40:46,269 --> 00:40:47,575
Yeah.

780
00:40:48,620 --> 00:40:50,448
<i>Rough day at the office, huh?</i>

781
00:40:53,189 --> 00:40:55,278
You can say that.

782
00:40:58,456 --> 00:41:00,240
Are the girls there?

783
00:41:00,327 --> 00:41:01,981
<i>- Can I talk to them?</i>
- Yeah.

784
00:41:01,981 --> 00:41:03,156
Yeah, uh, which one?

785
00:41:03,156 --> 00:41:04,940
<i>Just put me on speaker.</i>

786
00:41:04,940 --> 00:41:06,551
[girls talking quietly]

787
00:41:06,551 --> 00:41:08,161
It's falling apart.

788
00:41:08,161 --> 00:41:10,468
Girls, it's your mother.

789
00:41:10,468 --> 00:41:12,295
- [Charlie] <i>Hi!</i>
- [Kate] <i>Hi, Mom.</i>

790
00:41:14,820 --> 00:41:16,648
[Kate]
<i>Mom, are you okay?</i>

791
00:41:17,910 --> 00:41:19,346
[inhales deeply]

792
00:41:19,346 --> 00:41:21,043
[exhales]

793
00:41:21,130 --> 00:41:22,915
Hi, baby. I'm fine.

794
00:41:24,133 --> 00:41:24,960
<i>I'm good.</i>

795
00:41:26,222 --> 00:41:27,223
[Kate]
Are you sure?

796
00:41:28,181 --> 00:41:30,618
I'm...
[sniffles]

797
00:41:30,705 --> 00:41:32,185
I'm great, I'm great.

798
00:41:32,272 --> 00:41:34,013
How are you?

799
00:41:34,013 --> 00:41:35,231
We're making supper.

800
00:41:35,318 --> 00:41:36,798
<i>Oh, yeah, what's for supper?</i>

801
00:41:36,885 --> 00:41:38,321
Pizookie.

802
00:41:38,321 --> 00:41:40,280
<i>A what?</i>

803
00:41:40,367 --> 00:41:41,847
[Neal]
<i>Well, Mom,</i>

804
00:41:41,847 --> 00:41:43,892
<i>you take a whole batch
of cookie dough</i>

805
00:41:43,892 --> 00:41:46,025
<i>and you spread it out
in an iron skillet.</i>

806
00:41:46,025 --> 00:41:49,071
<i>And it makes a cookie
the size of a pizza.</i>

807
00:41:49,158 --> 00:41:50,159
<i>A pizookie.</i>

808
00:41:50,159 --> 00:41:51,421
[sniffles]

809
00:41:51,421 --> 00:41:53,859
That sounds... healthy.

810
00:41:53,859 --> 00:41:55,469
- [laughs]
- [Charlie] <i>It is</i>

811
00:41:55,469 --> 00:41:57,253
if you have ice cream with it.

812
00:41:57,253 --> 00:41:59,299
They make ice cream out of milk.

813
00:41:59,386 --> 00:42:01,214
<i>Boy, do they have you
trained, baby.</i>

814
00:42:01,214 --> 00:42:03,129
Oh, yeah, I'm aware.

815
00:42:04,304 --> 00:42:06,785
I sure wish I could have some.

816
00:42:06,785 --> 00:42:08,656
[Kate]
<i>You can.</i>

817
00:42:08,743 --> 00:42:10,571
<i>- When are you coming home?</i>
- [sniffling]

818
00:42:14,053 --> 00:42:16,403
Soon, baby.

819
00:42:16,403 --> 00:42:18,536
Soon.

820
00:42:22,278 --> 00:42:24,324
I love you.

821
00:42:24,324 --> 00:42:25,891
<i>- Love you.</i>
- [Charlie] <i>Love you, too.</i>

822
00:42:25,891 --> 00:42:27,675
- [Neal] <i>Love you, Mom.</i>
- [Charlie] <i>Bye-bye.</i>

823
00:42:27,675 --> 00:42:29,634
<i>♪ melancholy music</i>

824
00:42:29,634 --> 00:42:31,549
<i>♪</i>

825
00:43:01,709 --> 00:43:03,798
<i>♪</i>

826
00:43:19,379 --> 00:43:21,424
<i>♪ dramatic music ♪</i>

827
00:43:21,424 --> 00:43:23,557
<i>♪</i>

828
00:43:44,056 --> 00:43:46,101
<i>♪</i>

829
00:43:58,070 --> 00:44:03,553
<i>♪</i>

